+### 0.9.6_Hardened_1 language-conformance condition
+
+`0.9.6_Hardened_1` MUST NOT be declared conformant until all H10 conditions remain satisfied and
+repository evidence additionally proves that:
+
+1. equivalent borrow relationships represented by `Span`, `MutSpan`, `ref`, `ref mut`, `@view`
+   fields, Arena-backed views, `RefCell` guards, and foreign views receive equivalent safety decisions
+   where their semantic axes are equivalent;
+2. lifetime provenance and concrete storage identity remain distinct, and neither region equality nor
+   region inequality is used as a substitute for an overlap/disjointness proof;
+3. exact, trusted-declared, and conservative-unknown callable facts preserve both access and
+   field-to-region provenance, including generic, separately compiled, dynamic, and hot-reload target
+   sets;
+4. changing either callable summary rechecks affected callers and invalidates all dependent interface,
+   generic, and cache artifacts; stale metadata is a hard compiler failure;
+5. compiler-only capability, region, access-summary, and initialization-proof metadata is absent from
+   runtime layout, ABI, serialization, and hot-reload schemas;
+6. ordinary assignment, `Cell.set`, and `MaybeUninit.write`/`write_at` preserve their distinct ordering
+   contracts in MIR and generated code;
+7. `[ARN-10]` tests show successful `Default` construction, v1 process termination through `[PAN-1]`
+   on panic, no continuation after panic, no compiler-invented unwind path, and no observation of
+   post-panic Arena state;
+8. existing H10 safety regressions remain present and green; implementation-path consolidation is not
+   used to delete an adversarial test.
+
